title: The presidential year

@left_presidential_split
# prose-audit: Grade A — The nomination reconciliation and the candidate rollout are model work: every committee is named, the five-way aggregation is explained as arithmetic rather than alliance, and each leading campaign now holds its own page in the same styled field block the 2020 chapter uses. The five campaign operations resolve into consequences the player can read rather than a subtitle and a counter.
title: The presidential field opens
subtitle: Turn the nomination into a national campaign
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 25
order: 10
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/poland/cards/campaigning.webp
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 1 and election_2027_terminal = 0
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.pres_2025_left_candidate ||
    Q.pres_2025_left_candidate == "Undecided") {
    Q.pres_2025_left_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat";
}
Q.pres_2025_candidate = Q.pres_2025_left_candidate;
Q.pres_2025_active = 1;
Q.pres_2025_phase = "First-round campaign";
Q.pres_2025_round_one_done = 0;
Q.pres_2025_first_round_winner = 0;
Q.pres_2025_first_round_winner_share = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_done = 0;
Q.pres_2025_feedback_applied = 0;
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Not chosen";
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "none";
Q.pres_2025_winner = "";
Q.pres_2025_winner_key = "";
Q.pres_2025_hostile_president = 0;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength = 0;
if (!Q.pres_2025_ko_candidate ||
    Q.pres_2025_ko_candidate == "Undecided") {
    Q.pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Rafał Trzaskowski";
}
Q.pres_2025_ko_surname =
    Q.pres_2025_ko_candidate == "Radosław Sikorski" ? "Sikorski" :
    (Q.pres_2025_ko_candidate == "Barbara Nowacka" ? "Nowacka" :
        "Trzaskowski");
// Konfederacja chooses between its libertarian chair and the national wing's
// parliamentary face. The simulation key remains `mentzen` for save
// compatibility; the name on the ballot is live.
const mentzenNominationWeight = Math.max(
    10,
    Number(Q.konf_mentzenite_share) || 47
);
const bosakNominationWeight = Math.max(
    10,
    Number(Q.konf_nationalist_share) || 35
);
Q.pres_2025_konf_candidate =
    (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) *
        (mentzenNominationWeight + bosakNominationWeight) <
        mentzenNominationWeight
        ? "Sławomir Mentzen"
        : "Krzysztof Bosak";
Q.pres_2025_konf_surname =
    Q.pres_2025_konf_candidate == "Krzysztof Bosak" ? "Bosak" : "Mentzen";
// PiS runs through a civic committee because its own brand is damaged, but the
// name inside the committee is a live argument between its wings.
const pisWeights = {
    "Karol Nawrocki": 52,
    "Mateusz Morawiecki":
        Q.morawiecki_advisor || Q.morawiecki_left_defectors
            ? 0
            : 16 + Math.max(0, (Number(Q.pis_solidarist_share) || 55) - 55) * 0.9,
    "Przemysław Czarnek":
        14 + Math.max(0, (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 32) - 32) * 0.7,
    "Tobiasz Bocheński":
        12 + Math.max(0, (Number(Q.pis_market_hardliner_share) || 45) - 45) * 0.9
};
const pisNames = Object.keys(pisWeights);
const pisTotal = pisNames.reduce(function(sum, name) {
    return sum + pisWeights[name];
}, 0);
let pisDraw = (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * pisTotal;
Q.pres_2025_right_candidate = "Karol Nawrocki";
for (const name of pisNames) {
    pisDraw -= pisWeights[name];
    if (pisDraw <= 0) {
        Q.pres_2025_right_candidate = name;
        break;
    }
}
Q.pres_2025_right_surname =
    Q.pres_2025_right_candidate == "Mateusz Morawiecki" ? "Morawiecki" :
    (Q.pres_2025_right_candidate == "Przemysław Czarnek" ? "Czarnek" :
    (Q.pres_2025_right_candidate == "Tobiasz Bocheński" ? "Bocheński" :
        "Nawrocki"));
// Poland 2050 sends its founder unless its market-liberal wing has grown
// strong enough to argue that a banker's campaign travels further than a
// television moralist's.
const petruWeight =
    Math.max(0, ((Number(Q.p2050_right_score) || 52) - 52) * 3.2) +
    (Q.p2050_leader && Q.p2050_leader != "Szymon Hołownia" ? 45 : 0) +
    (Q.p2050_internal_split ? 12 : 0);
Q.pres_2025_centre_candidate =
    Q.p2050_2023_exclusion_comeback_done
        ? "Szymon Hołownia"
        : (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * (100 + petruWeight) > 100
        ? "Ryszard Petru"
        : "Szymon Hołownia";
Q.pres_2025_centre_surname =
    Q.pres_2025_centre_candidate == "Ryszard Petru" ? "Petru" : "Hołownia";
// Kanał Zero's candidacy is normally a critique of campaigning rather than a
// campaign. Occasionally the audience decides to vote.
const stanowskiRoll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const stanowskiScale = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
Q.pres_2025_stanowski_breakout = stanowskiRoll < 0.07 ? 1 : 0;
Q.pres_2025_stanowski_surge = Q.pres_2025_stanowski_breakout
    ? 7 + stanowskiScale * 12
    : 0;
const razemFederated25 =
    String(Q.left_merger_structure || "") == "federation" &&
    Q.merger_razem_present &&
    String(Q.razem_org_status || "") != "departed";
const razemOutside25 =
    Q.razem_split || Q.razem_party_formed || !Q.razem_in_left;
const razemCampaignStrength25 = razemOutside25
    ? Math.max(
        Number(Q.razem_exit_strength) || 0,
        Number(Q.razem_vote_intent) || 0
    )
    : Number(Q.razem_strength) || 0;
const razemCohesive25 =
    Q.razem_cooperation_protocol || Q.razem_breakaway_protected ||
    (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) >= 55;
const razemRupture25 = (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) >= 45;
Q.pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible =
    !razemFederated25 && !razemCohesive25 && razemRupture25 &&
    razemCampaignStrength25 >= 8 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.pres_2025_left_candidate == "Adrian Zandberg") {
    Q.pres_2025_united_left = 1;
    Q.pres_2025_razem_candidate = "None";
}
if (!Q.pres_2025_united_left && Q.pres_2025_razem_separate_eligible) {
    Q.pres_2025_razem_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg";
    if (!Q.pres_2025_nomination_method ||
        Q.pres_2025_nomination_method == "Not chosen") {
        Q.pres_2025_nomination_method = "Separate candidacies";
        Q.pres_2025_unity_effect = 0;
    }
} else {
    Q.pres_2025_united_left = 1;
    Q.pres_2025_razem_candidate = "None";
    if (Q.pres_2025_nomination_method == "Separate candidacies") {
        Q.pres_2025_nomination_method = "Common Left nomination";
    } else if (Q.pres_2025_nomination_method == "New Left national council") {
        Q.pres_2025_nomination_method = "Common Left national council";
    } else if (!Q.pres_2025_nomination_method ||
        Q.pres_2025_nomination_method == "Not chosen") {
        Q.pres_2025_nomination_method = "Inherited common nomination";
        Q.pres_2025_unity_effect = 0;
    }
}
Q.pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining = 2;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_work = 0;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_rights = 0;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_counties = 0;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_constitution = 0;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_left_ground = 0;
Q.pres_2025_field_seen = 0;
Q.pres_2025_debate_bonus = 0;
Q.pres_2025_debate_shift = 0;
Q.pres_2025_debate_strategy = "Not chosen";
Q.pres_2025_debate_upset = "None";
Q.pres_2025_support_actions_remaining = 2;
Q.pres_2025_support_holownia = 0;
Q.pres_2025_support_committees = 0;
Q.pres_2025_support_stanowski = 0;
Q.pres_2025_support_movements = 0;
Q.pres_2025_support_radical = 0;
Q.pres_2025_support_left = 0;
Q.pres_2025_support_turnout = 0;
Q.pres_2025_support_release = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_push_bonus = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_campaign = "Not chosen";
Q.pres_2025_runoff_final_push = "Not chosen";
Q.pres_2025_runoff_calc_mode = "result";
Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_name = "No candidate";
Q.pres_2025_torun_route = "none";
Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key = "none";
Q.pres_2025_torun_target_name = "No candidate";
Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line = "No written line";
Q.pres_2025_torun_breach = "No breach";
Q.pres_2025_runoff_breach_shift = 0;
Q.pres_2025_morawiecki_push = "No personnel bargain";
for (const id of [
    "ko", "right", "left", "razem", "mentzen",
    "braun", "holownia", "stanowski", "other"
]) {
    Q["pres_2025_rival_shift_" + id] = 0;
    Q["pres_2025_trade_boost_" + id] = 0;
}
const pollIds = [
    "ko", "right", "left", "razem", "mentzen",
    "braun", "holownia", "stanowski", "other"
];
for (const id of pollIds) {
    Q["pres_2025_open_noise_" + id] =
        (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 - 0.5) *
        (Q.hard_mode ? 1.8 : 1.5);
    Q["pres_2025_track_noise_" + id] =
        (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 - 0.5) *
        (Q.hard_mode ? 1.4 : 1.1);
}
Q.news_headline =
    Q.pres_2025_united_left
        ? "A common Left candidate opens the presidential year"
        : Q.pres_2025_left_candidate +
            " and Zandberg prepare to measure two Left strategies";
Q.pres_2025_r1_turnout_shock =
    (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 - 0.5) *
    (Q.hard_mode ? 1.4 : 1.0);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_turnout_shock =
    (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 - 0.5) *
    (Q.hard_mode ? 1.6 : 1.2);
// The inter-round poll and the second ballot are drawn once, in advance, so
// that the tracking poll cannot be re-read until it agrees with the campaign.
Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_shock =
    ((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 2 - 1) *
    (Q.hard_mode ? 1.05 : 0.9);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_result_shock =
    ((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 2 - 1) *
    (Q.hard_mode ? 1.25 : 1.15);
!}

= January 2025 — Government record or opposition programme

[? if pres_2025_united_left: **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]** carries the
common nomination, but New Left's ministers and Razem's opposition organisers
still disagree over what the candidacy is meant to prove: delivery from office
or freedom from coalition compromise.?]
[? if not pres_2025_united_left: New Left has chosen **[+
pres_2025_left_candidate +]**. [? if pres_2025_left_candidate = "Magdalena
Biejat": The deputy marshal of the Senate brings a campaign built around
housing, care and cooperation.?][? if pres_2025_left_candidate = "Agnieszka
Dziemianowicz-Bąk": The former labour minister brings a campaign built around
work, schools and public services.?] Razem answers with its co-founder and
economic spokesman <span class="party-razem"><b>Adrian Zandberg</b></span>, who can ask why office has left so much
undone.?]

[? if pres_2025_united_left: One name on the ballot does not erase the
organisational split. Local branches share volunteers, while ministers and
opposition organisers still want the candidacy to prove different things.?][?
if not pres_2025_united_left: The split is not merely two names on a ballot.
Local branches share volunteers, trade unions want a reliable transfer in the
second round, and both campaigns need the same younger renters without allowing
the other to define the whole Left.?] We must decide whether competition stops
at the office door.

- @left_campaign_shared
- @left_campaign_compete
- @left_campaign_last_offer

@left_campaign_shared
title: Build a shared field operation across the Left
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Preserves transfer channels without hiding disagreement.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot finance shared organisers.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength += 4;
Q.razem_cooperation += 5;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.news_headline = Q.pres_2025_united_left
    ? "The common Left campaign unites its field operation"
    : "Two Left campaigns share organisers and anti-right mobilisation";
!}

[? if pres_2025_united_left: Ministers, Razem organisers and local branches
share rooms and canvass lists behind **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]**, while
retaining the right to argue over the programme. The common nomination gains a
field organisation broad enough to make its claim of unity credible.?][? if not
pres_2025_united_left: **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]** and Zandberg keep
separate headquarters and programmes but share rooms, canvass lists and a
promise not to strand the other's voters in a runoff. District organisers gain
a campaign they can survive even when their preferred candidate loses.?]

- @presidential_field_2025: Meet the presidential field

@left_campaign_compete
title: Let government delivery compete openly with Razem's opposition
subtitle: A sharper campaign wins attention but teaches the two Left camps to treat each other as rivals.
on-arrival: pres_2025_campaign_strength += 2; media_capacity += 2; razem_cooperation -= 5; razem_dissent += 3; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "The presidential campaign becomes a referendum on Left strategy"

[? if pres_2025_united_left: Ministers present **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate
+]** as proof that office can deliver, while Razem organisers use the same
candidacy to attack coalition compromises. Coverage improves because the
argument is real; voters may wonder which of the two programmes the common
nominee would actually carry.?][? if not pres_2025_united_left: The governing
Left puts ministers and delivered programmes behind **[+
pres_2025_left_candidate +]**; Razem sends Zandberg into workplaces and studios
to prosecute the compromises. Coverage improves, as does the chance that local
members learn to see the other campaign as the opponent rather than the
reserve.?]

- @presidential_field_2025: Meet the presidential field

@left_campaign_last_offer
title: Make one final common-candidate offer to Zandberg
subtitle: Requires substantial Razem cooperation.
view-if: pres_2025_united_left = 0
choose-if: razem_cooperation >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: The split has become part of both campaigns' legitimacy.
on-arrival: pres_2025_left_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; pres_2025_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; pres_2025_razem_candidate = "None"; pres_2025_united_left = 1; pres_2025_nomination_method = "Late leadership withdrawal"; pres_2025_unity_effect = -0.8; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 6; razem_cooperation += 4; barons_dissent += 7; spring_dissent += 4; party_unity += 3; news_headline = "The Left makes Zandberg its common presidential candidate"

Zandberg receives the common nomination, replacing the nominee chosen in
December. That candidate's network and every team already assigned to a joint
campaign are asked to transfer their organisers.
The old apparatus and the Wiosna inheritance have not suddenly become Zandberg
loyalists; unity arrives as a bargain they will expect his programme to repay.

- @presidential_field_2025: Meet the presidential field

