= April 2025 — Who will defend the pilot?

[? if shorter_time_pilot_active: Employers and public institutions can apply
to a Labour-Ministry trial of shorter hours without cutting pay. Labour
Minister **[+ labor_minister +]** of **[+ labor_minister_party +]** can decide
whether unions help govern each workplace trial and whether independent
evaluators own the evidence.?]
[? if not shorter_time_pilot_active: Lewica does not control the Labour
Ministry, so no national trial starts automatically. Labour-policy organiser
<span class="party-lewica"><b>Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk</b></span>, trade unions and willing employers can draft a
pilot and collect voluntary evidence, but they cannot turn participation into
a government programme.?]

Workers need shorter hours without hidden work intensification. Employers want
subsidy and flexibility; the Finance Ministry wants productivity figures before
the promise expands. The pilot will either create institutions capable of
defending a later reform or become a slogan a later minister can bury.

