= 16 April 2025 — A campaign enters the ward

Far-right MEP and presidential candidate <span class="party-korona"><b>Grzegorz Braun</b></span> enters the Oleśnica
County Hospital with supporters after a lawful abortion in a high-risk
pregnancy. He calls his action a citizen's detention of **Dr Gizela Jagielska**,
the gynaecologist who provided the care. Jagielska says she is kept from
leaving an office and treating patients for more than an hour; prosecutors
open a separate investigation into alleged unlawful detention, physical
contact and insults.

Patients and staff need the ward returned to clinical work. Jagielska needs
counsel rather than politicians speaking in her place, and investigators need
unedited records rather than campaign footage. This is not a vote on anybody's
guilt: Lewica can protect the institution and its evidence, seek a common
hospital rule, or turn the raid into the centre of the abortion campaign.

- @braun_hospital_evidence
- @braun_hospital_joint
- @braun_hospital_campaign

@braun_hospital_evidence
title: Fund staff protection, victim counsel and a preserved evidence file
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Protect staff and preserve a case that does not belong to the party.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot staff the legal and clinical support team.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; braun_hospital_response = "Evidence, victim counsel and clinical continuity"; braun_legal_preparation += 5; braun_martyrdom -= 1; public_trust += 2; public_sector_support += 2; feminist_trust += 2; news_headline = "Hospital records and victim counsel replace the raid's edited footage"

Counsel takes Jagielska's instructions, hospital security preserves access
logs and full recordings, and replacement staff keep patients from paying for
the disruption. Braun can still campaign on the confrontation, but later legal
decisions will begin from evidence the party neither edited nor owns.

- @poland_event_queue: File the protected evidence record

@braun_hospital_joint
title: Demand one cross-party rule for threats and obstruction in hospitals
subtitle: Defend clinical work across parties without asking Parliament to pronounce guilt.
on-arrival: braun_hospital_response = "Cross-party hospital-safety and evidence protocol"; braun_legal_preparation += 3; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 3; ko_relation += 2; p2050_relation += 1; braun_martyrdom += 1; news_headline = "The democratic parties defend clinical work without prejudging the case"

Lewica, KO and Poland 2050 agree that no campaign may obstruct a ward and that
police, prosecutors and hospital management will publish the same preservation
protocol. Staff gain a rule without a parliamentary verdict on guilt. Braun
calls the common front proof that the establishment has united against him.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the hospital-safety compact

