    " makes the democratic camp answer for unfinished rights promises";
!}

The record is read out as a list with dates attached: what was promised in
October 2023, what reached committee, what was withdrawn the week before a vote
and on whose insistence. [? if left_in_government: It is an awkward list to read
from inside the coalition, and the nominee reads it anyway, which is the part
that registers.?][? if not left_in_government: It is the list an opposition
exists to read, and nobody on the platform can claim it is invented.?]

**[+ pres_2025_ko_surname +]** answers that these are parliamentary matters.
That is precisely
the sentence the list was constructed to draw out of him, and it will be
replayed more often than anything either of them said about rights.

- @pres25_debate_questions: The all-candidate format opens the questions

@pres25_rights_procedure
title: [+ pres_2025_rights_procedure_title +]
subtitle: Constitutionally safe and politically narrow; movements hear another deferral.
on-arrival: pres_2025_debate_score += 1.2; pres_2025_debate_rights_line = pres_2025_rights_procedure_title; constitutional_restraint += 2; feminist_trust -= 3; progressives_dissent += 3; pres_2025_debate_round = 4; news_headline = "The Left narrows the rights answer to presidential procedure"

The answer is about process: a president receives a bill, a president has
twenty-one days, a president may refer a statute to a court that must be
repaired first. Every clause of it is true and none of it says what the pen
would do.

**[+ pres_2025_right_surname +]** does not bother to attack it. The women's
organisations that spent the
spring supplying the campaign with volunteers hear the same deferral they have
heard since the autumn of 2023, and some of them stop returning calls before
the week is out.

- @pres25_debate_questions: The all-candidate format opens the questions

@pres25_debate_questions
title: Debate IV — choose whom to question
new-page: true

In the all-candidate format each campaign chooses opponents and the organisers
draw another pairing. A question can expose a rival, but it also names the
contest our campaign wants viewers to remember.

[? if not pres_2025_united_left: Zandberg is a legitimate rival for the same
Left electorate. Questioning him turns the organisational split into the
night's central argument.?][? if pres_2025_united_left: Zandberg is part of our
common campaign and cannot be selected as an opponent. The question must cross
an actual campaign boundary.?]

- @pres25_question_nawrocki
- @pres25_question_mentzen
- @pres25_question_trzaskowski
- @pres25_question_zandberg

@pres25_question_nawrocki
title: Ask [+ pres_2025_right_surname +] which PiS appointment would ever be refused
subtitle: Makes the independence of the PiS-backed candidacy the test.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_debate_score += 2.5;
Q.pres_2025_debate_question_line = Q.pres_2025_right_surname +
    " must define independence from the party that built the campaign";
Q.pres_2025_debate_target = "right";
