= 1 June 2025 — Poland chooses the Palace

Turnout: **[+ pres_2025_runoff_turnout +]%** ·
Valid votes: **[+ pres_2025_runoff_valid_votes_display +]**

**[+ pres_2025_runoff_a_name +] [+ pres_2025_runoff_a_share +]%**
([+ pres_2025_runoff_votes_a_display +])  
**[+ pres_2025_runoff_b_name +] [+ pres_2025_runoff_b_share +]%**
([+ pres_2025_runoff_votes_b_display +])

Margin: **[+ pres_2025_runoff_margin +] points**

President-elect: **[+ pres_2025_winner +]**.

The eliminated electorates did not transfer as party leaders instructed.
Lewica's line — **[+ pres_2025_transfer_strategy +]** — opened doors and moved
organisers; voters still decided whether to walk through them. The last
fortnight was spent on **[+ pres_2025_runoff_final_push +]**, and no campaign
will ever know what the other version of it would have produced.

Every camp will claim it supplied the decisive voters; the certified count
gives the presidential pen to one person for the next five years.

[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "left": Lewica has won the Palace. **[+
pres_2025_winner +]** must now become President of the Republic without turning
the office into party headquarters. [? if left_in_government: Our ministers
and caucus will be judged by whether a friendly signature produces actual
law.?][? if not left_in_government: Our caucus must prove that a Left president
can widen the party's reach without treating the Palace as an opposition
headquarters.?]?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "razem": **[+ pres_2025_winner +]** reaches the
Palace through Razem's opposition campaign. The wider Left gains a president
and a new internal centre of gravity: New Left must work with a rival who can
sign its bills and publicly expose their compromises.?]
