@umamusume_aftermath
title: The final straight
face-image: img/poland/events/umamusume-rice-shower.webp
new-page: true

= One clean run

[? if umamusume_release_response = "Organiser school": By morning, every
district has a training plan, a rest cycle and a closing-straight target. The
organisers embrace the structure. The old guard requests that nobody ever call
candidate selection a *scouting ticket* again.?]

[? if umamusume_release_response = "Consumer-protection bill": The draft does
not ban the game. It requires clear odds, legible prices, spending controls and
a route for parents and players to challenge manipulative design. Fans argue
over the details; lawyers quietly replace every horse pun with statutory
language. It remains a proposal until Parliament acts.?]

[? if umamusume_release_response = "Protected leisure": There is no reaction
clip, no branded stream and no emergency horseshoe logo. The staff go home.
Several return tomorrow with more stamina. Nobody can prove the restraint hurt
the republic.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Return to politics

@third_way_ends
# prose-audit: Grade B — The expiry itself is strong and the successor branches are properly authored. The PSL accounting scene then opens by printing "PSL's leverage is [+ psl_ratchet_score +]/100" — a raw model score shown to the player, which the interaction standard rules out even when, as here, the causes are listed afterwards.
title: Third Way reaches its expiry date
subtitle: Its own cohesion and accumulated disputes decide whether the pact survives
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kosiniak.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 25
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month >= 6 and coalition_confidence_2025_done = 1 and third_way_split = 0
on-arrival: {!
const thirdWayRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 13) - 6;
let splitPressure =
    46 +
    Math.max(0, 55 - (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 0)) -
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 0) - 55) * 0.35 +
    (Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.28 +
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.24 +
    Math.max(0, 35 - (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0)) * 0.15 +
    Math.max(0, 35 - (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 0)) * 0.12 +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) - 12) * 0.35 +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) * 0.08 +
    thirdWayRoll;
if (!Q.government_has_confidence) splitPressure += 8;
Q.third_way_split_pressure = Math.round(splitPressure);
Q.third_way_split = splitPressure > 52 ? 1 : 0;
Q.third_way_active = Q.third_way_split ? 0 : 1;
Q.third_way_cohesion += Q.third_way_split ? -25 : 8;
Q.third_way_outgoing_leadership =
    "Szymon Hołownia and Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz as joint electoral principals";
Q.third_way_incoming_leadership = Q.third_way_split
    ? "Hołownia for Poland 2050 and Kosiniak-Kamysz for PSL, negotiating separately"
    : "Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz under a renewed, looser pact";
Q.news_headline = Q.third_way_split
    ? (Q.government_party == "pis"
        ? "PSL and Poland 2050 end Third Way from opposition"
        : (Q.government_has_confidence
            ? "PSL and Poland 2050 end Third Way while both remain in the parliamentary bargain"
            : "PSL and Poland 2050 end Third Way inside a government-formation crisis"))
    : "PSL and Poland 2050 renew Third Way after a close internal reckoning";
!}

= June 2025 — One deadline, two possible futures

The four-election pact has run its course. PSL's county barons and agrarian
conservatives want an independent survival strategy; Poland 2050's founder
loyalists and reform wing want freedom from PSL's social-policy vetoes. Their
poor presidential campaigns mean the joint brand can no longer hide the fact
that the two parties answer to different electorates.

[? if third_way_split: The principals conclude that separate parties now offer
better survival odds. Lewica cannot veto that decision; it can only choose how
to deal with the successor clubs.?]
[? if not third_way_split: The pressure falls just short. Both principals renew
the pact, but only as a looser electoral agreement that preserves more party
autonomy.?]

[? if government_party = "pis": PSL and Poland 2050 are opposition parties.
Their brand decision changes electoral coordination and future majority
building; it does not renegotiate membership in the PiS cabinet.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and government_has_confidence: The cabinet survived the confidence vote, so
the end of an electoral brand becomes an immediate renegotiation among parties
that still supply its majority.?]
[? if government_party != "pis" and not government_has_confidence: The cabinet has already lost confidence.
Third Way dissolves inside formation talks, where each successor party can
sell its seats separately.?]

[? if government_party = "pis": For Lewica, opposition coordination now
requires separate agreements with PSL and Poland 2050. Playing them against
each other may help one vote and destroy the next common majority.?][? if
government_party != "pis": For Lewica, coalition management now requires
separate majorities with PSL and Poland 2050. Playing them against each other
may win one bill and destroy the government's remaining trust.?]

- @td_bilateral
- @td_psl
- @td_rebuild
- @td_renew
- @td_loose_pact

@td_bilateral
title: Replace the bloc with separate written agreements
