= August 2025 — The date belongs to the Constitution

The official count gives <span class="party-pis"><b>[+ pres_2025_right_candidate +]</b></span> the presidency and the Supreme
Court has ruled on the election's validity. Complaints about individual
precincts can still be examined; Sejm Marshal <span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span> does not
gain authority to recertify the national result.

People Hołownia will not name urge him to withhold the National Assembly on
6 August. If the outgoing President's term expires before **[+
pres_2025_right_surname +]** takes the oath, they
argue, Article 131 lets the Marshal temporarily discharge presidential duties.
No evidence establishes a collective coalition plan. The proposal is now in
the room, however, and every party must decide whether to kill it, discipline
it into lawful review or try it.

[? if left_in_government: Lewica's ministers can lend the proposal coalition
authority or make the Council of Ministers reject it in writing.?][? if not
left_in_government: Lewica holds no cabinet office. It can expose the approach,
support a lawful evidence process or add parliamentary votes and public cover
to the delay; it cannot order the Marshal or the Supreme Court.?]

- @oath_fixed_date_2025
- @oath_audit_2025
- @oath_delay_2025
- @oath_acting_window_2025

