The sitting is not convened. The outgoing President's term expires and Hołownia claims that the
failure to assume office activates the Marshal's temporary duties. **[+
pres_2025_right_surname +]**,
PiS and much of the legal profession answer that the Marshal manufactured the
very obstacle on which his claim depends.

The manoeuvre has therefore worked in the narrowest sense: no elected
President occupies the Palace and government lawyers route urgent papers to a
disputed acting authority. It cannot award Hołownia a term or invalidate the
count. EU partners and Washington keep treaty channels open but postpone
senior decisions until Poland identifies one constitutional signature.

- @poland_event_queue: Enter the interregnum's compulsory end

