= August 2025 — The pen changes hands

[? if pres_2025_oath_crisis = 3: The interregnum ends because it cannot
manufacture a different electoral judgment, a durable presidential act or a
coalition willing to defend it. Hołownia convenes the National Assembly under
threat of removal. [? if pres_2025_oath_strategy = "Disputed acts during the interregnum": Courts freeze the appointments and statute signed during the disputed window; their legal-dualism cost remains after the office changes hands.?][? if pres_2025_oath_strategy != "Disputed acts during the interregnum": The temporary acting claim produces no presidential act before the elected winner arrives.?]?]

**[+ president_name +]** takes the oath as President of the Republic while
Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** still depends on the same Sejm. The
ceremony changes who may sign, veto and refer a bill; it does not silently move
a single deputy or ministry.

[? if pres_2025_incumbent and pres_2025_winner = "Rafał Trzaskowski":
Trzaskowski begins a second term. The oath confirms that five years of
cohabitation were a governing fact, not an interlude: his veto record, signed
opposition bills and the PiS stress-versus-rally balance now carry into the new
Sejm cycle.?]
[? if pres_2025_hostile_president: The governing coalition still lacks the
three-fifths majority needed to override vetoes. Every labour, equality and
judicial bill now needs a Palace bargain, a workaround or a public defeat.?]
[? if not pres_2025_hostile_president: A friendly signature removes one veto
wall. It does not remove PSL, the Senate timetable, judicial dualism or the
coalition's own internal vetoes.?]

[? if left_in_government and caretaker_government = 0:
Lewica must decide whether its ministers negotiate every flagship text with
the Palace or turn each veto into the next campaign.?][? if not left_in_government or
caretaker_government = 1: Lewica cannot
speak for the cabinet. It can offer the President public hearings on its own
bills or build an opposition record of every signature, veto and referral.?]

- @palace_channels
- @palace_mandate
- @palace_opposition_channels
- @palace_opposition_veto_campaign

