= September 2025 — Security is also a budget

Russian drones cross Polish airspace during another attack on Ukraine. Polish
and allied crews scramble, while Defence Minister **[+ defence_minister +]** of
**[+ defence_minister_party +]** must explain what was detected, intercepted
and allowed to fall. NATO's Eastern Sentry response makes reinforcement
available; it does not decide what Poland buys or what civilians receive.

Air-force personnel need systems that work. Eastern mayors need warnings,
shelters and a chain of command that reaches below Warsaw. Lewica's voters also
know that every procurement promise competes with hospitals, housing and local
services. We can back the military layer, insist that civilians share the
budget, or make verified evidence the condition of escalation.

- @drones_nato
- @drones_civil
- @drones_restraint

@drones_nato
title: Back NATO reinforcement and air-defence procurement
subtitle: Make an unambiguous allied commitment and accept a new claim on the public budget.
