= September 2025 — A movement after its founder

[? if pres_2025_oath_crisis = 3: Hołownia enters the succession after his
attempt to withhold the presidential oath collapsed. Poland 2050 now carries
the foreign isolation, disputed-acting-power claim and coalition defections
created from its founder's parliamentary office.?]

[? if president_name = "Szymon Hołownia": Founder <span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span> has
taken the presidential oath. The Palace cannot double as his movement's daily
party headquarters, so Poland 2050 must elect a successor.?]
[? if president_name != "Szymon Hołownia": Founder <span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span> says
he will leave the leadership while Poland 2050 still holds cabinet and
parliamentary offices.?]
[? if p2050_2023_exclusion_comeback_done and president_name != "Szymon Hołownia":
The independent relaunch gave Hołownia a
credible case for staying. This time it was not enough: the movement's own
delegates decide that the founder's renewed ceiling has been reached.?]

<span class="party-p2050"><b>Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz</b></span>, the party figure identified with EU funds and
state capacity, offers an organisation that can survive through policy and
ministerial competence. <span class="party-p2050"><b>Paulina Hennig-Kloska</b></span>, its climate-policy
ministerial figure, speaks for green centrists. Hołownia's personal loyalists
ask whether either current can retain the volunteers who joined a movement
rather than a conventional party.

[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Szymon Hołownia" and president_name !=
"Szymon Hołownia" and third_way_split: Hołownia's presidential defeat and the
end of Third Way have removed both the founder's electoral magic and the
party's threshold shelter.?]
[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Szymon Hołownia" and president_name !=
"Szymon Hołownia" and third_way_active: Hołownia's presidential defeat leaves
a surviving Third Way dependent on a partner whose own command is changing.?]
[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Ryszard Petru" and pres_2025_winner_key !=
"holownia" and third_way_split: Petru's presidential defeat and the end of
Third Way leave Hołownia retiring from a movement that has lost both its
market-liberal electoral test and its threshold shelter.?]
[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Ryszard Petru" and pres_2025_winner_key !=
"holownia" and third_way_active: Petru's presidential defeat leaves the
surviving Third Way dependent on a founder who did not carry its ballot and is
now surrendering daily command.?]
[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Ryszard Petru" and pres_2025_winner_key =
"holownia": Petru's victory gives Poland 2050 the Palace without preserving
Hołownia's daily command of the party; succession now has to divide those two
sources of authority.?]
[? if pres_2025_stanowski_breakout = 1: Stanowski's presidential breakthrough
has also occupied the anti-party electorate Poland 2050 once treated as its
reserve. The successor inherits a competitor with a larger channel, a measured
vote and no coalition record to defend.?]
Ministers and MPs need a successor before uncertainty becomes a defection race.

Lewica can keep channels open across the contest or spend political capital on
the camp most likely to turn coalition bargains into delivery. Neutrality
protects the relationship; intervention helps choose who owns it.

- @holownia_neutral
- @holownia_partner

