on-arrival: last_independence_march_year = 2025; far_right_street_capacity += 4; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -5; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 6; public_mood_pending_national_security_salience += 5

= November 2025 — Three rivals on the right

**Sławomir Mentzen's** Konfederacja, **Grzegorz Braun's** Crown movement and
PiS all arrive in Warsaw wanting to own the same national symbols. Their
competition does not make the street safer: nationalist organisers can push
one another toward the slogan or confrontation most likely to dominate the
broadcast.

Lewica is no longer improvising its first response. Civic organisers remember
the alternative celebrations we built; anti-fascists remember our counter-
marches; lawyers, police and minority groups remember whether monitoring kept
people safe. A social-patriotic current also wants to enter the main march and
deny the right exclusive ownership of the flag. Whichever line we repeat will
inherit trained people—and promises they expect us to keep.

- @ind25_civic
- @ind25_join
- @ind25_security
- @ind25_counter

@ind25_civic
title: Expand the civic-independence alternative
subtitle: [? if civic_independence_investment >= 3: The permanent network now funds the march itself. No resource cost.?][? if civic_independence_investment < 3: Cost: 1 resource.?]
