@social_patriot_leadership_2025
# prose-audit: Grade A — The three routes now differ in what the organisation becomes: a party with a leader whose cultural positions nobody voted on, a council that governs well and cannot be interviewed, or a bureau seat bought with the freedom to be simply against things.
title: Lewica Patriotyczna chooses a national leadership
subtitle: Matysiak, regional organisers and the common Left contest control of the new organisation
face-image: img/poland/events/left-congress.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 25
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 11 and matysiak_resolution_done = 0 and social_patriot_active = 1

= November 2025 — An organisation needs a leadership

Lewica Patriotyczna has branches, its own policy work and referrals from
regional welfare organisers. <span class="party-razem"><b>Paulina Matysiak</b></span> offers a recognisable
developmental leadership. The founding council argues that the organisation
should not exchange SLD inheritance for another personality. The common Left
wants a chair it can keep inside one electoral family.

- @social_patriot_leader_matysiak
- @social_patriot_leader_council
- @social_patriot_leader_compact

@social_patriot_leader_matysiak
title: Elect Matysiak as national chair
subtitle: A clear developmental face strengthens the organisation and alarms progressives.
on-arrival: matysiak_resolution_done = 1; matysiak_party = "Lewica Patriotyczna"; matysiak_status = "Leader of Lewica Patriotyczna"; social_patriot_leader = "Paulina Matysiak"; social_patriot_strength += 4; social_patriot_cohesion += 5; progressive_credibility -= 3; progressives_dissent += 4; rural_support += 2; news_headline = "Matysiak becomes chair of Lewica Patriotyczna"

Matysiak takes the chair and the organisation acquires a face the television
studios already know. Within a fortnight the branch secretaries stop describing
themselves as a network and start describing themselves as a party with a
leader, which is a different thing to be.

The regional founders who built it out of welfare offices and parish halls get
a national profile they could not have produced themselves, and a leader whose
positions on abortion and church schools were never voted on by any of them.
Our progressives read the result as the developmental current acquiring a
standing army.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the leadership

@social_patriot_leader_council
title: Retain the regional founding council
subtitle: Stronger local ownership, slower national recognition.
on-arrival: matysiak_resolution_done = 1; matysiak_party = "Lewica Patriotyczna"; matysiak_status = "Social-Patriot organiser"; social_patriot_leader = "regional founding council"; social_patriot_local_organisation += 7; social_patriot_cohesion += 3; local_network += 3; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica Patriotyczna retains its regional collective leadership"

The founding council keeps command, which means the organisation continues to
be run by the people who know which county needs what. Decisions are slower and
better grounded; nobody in Warsaw can commit the network to a position its
branches have not discussed.

It also means Lewica Patriotyczna has no single voice to put on television.
Matysiak stays a prominent supporter rather than a chair, and every national
argument about what the current stands for gets answered by whichever regional
organiser a producer managed to reach.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the leadership

@social_patriot_leader_compact
title: Bind its leadership into the common Left bureau
subtitle: Unity rises, but the new organisation surrenders some autonomy.
on-arrival: matysiak_resolution_done = 1; social_patriot_leader = "joint Lewica Patriotyczna bureau"; social_patriot_dissent -= 6; social_patriot_cohesion -= 2; social_patriot_list_dependence += 8; party_unity += 4; barons_dissent += 3; news_headline = "Lewica Patriotyczna accepts a joint leadership compact"

The leadership is written into the common Left's bureau: a seat, a vote and an
obligation to bring disputes inside rather than to the press. The current gains
standing in the party it grew out of and gives up the freedom to be simply
against things.

Its organisers accept the trade with visible reluctance. They joined something
that felt like a corrective to the party apparatus and have just been made part
of it, and the first time the bureau overrules them they will remember which
signature put them in the room.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the leadership

@marriage_eu_2025
# prose-audit: Grade B — The CJEU judgment now follows married couples into registries, names Lewica's live executive limits and distinguishes recognition, equality legislation, cultural retreat and delay on every route.
title: Europe requires recognition of EU same-sex marriages
subtitle: Administrative recognition arrives before domestic marriage equality
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 24
order: 21
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/poland/cards/equality-bill.webp
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 11 and marriage_reform_stage < 3
on-arrival: european_judgment_compliance += 3; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 16; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 8; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 8; news_headline = "An EU judgment forces a practical equality decision"

= November 2025 — Recognition is not a full marriage statute

The Court of Justice of the European Union rules that Poland must recognise a
same-sex marriage lawfully concluded in another member state when EU rights
depend on it. Married couples now carry a European judgment to Polish
registries, tax offices and benefit administrators; they still do not possess
a Polish marriage-equality statute.

[? if left_in_government: Equality Minister **[+ equality_minister +]** of
**[+ equality_minister_party +]** can make the judgment usable through national
guidance. Lewica can also ask PSL leader <span class="party-psl"><b>Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz</b></span> and
President **[+ president_name +]** whether recognition should become equal
marriage.?][? if not left_in_government: Lewica cannot instruct national
registries. It can publish a model, support litigation and force Parliament to
choose whether European recognition remains the only marriage route available
to Polish same-sex couples.?]

- @marriage_implement
- @marriage_bill
- @marriage_registry_truce
- @marriage_delay
- @marriage_opposition_guidance

@marriage_implement
title: Issue immediate registry guidance and defend EU rights
subtitle: Give couples usable documents now and take responsibility for a fight with PSL and the Palace.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: minority_safety += 5; progressive_credibility += 4; european_judgment_compliance += 5; psl_relation -= 3; president_relation -= 2; news_headline = "Registries receive a rule before Parliament finds a majority"

National guidance tells registries which foreign marriages to enter and tells
administrators which family rights follow. Couples gain documents they can use
without beginning a new case in every office. PSL and the Palace object to the
scope, but the government owns compliance rather than outsourcing it to litigants.

- @poland_event_queue: File immediate recognition guidance

@marriage_bill
title: Use the ruling to introduce full marriage equality
subtitle: Refuse to make cross-border recognition the final settlement and reopen the domestic equality fight.
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 7; feminist_trust += 3; psl_relation -= 10; government_coalition_dissent += 8; president_relation -= 5; far_right_agenda += 5; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 14; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 10; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 9; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 10; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 9 if public_climate_progressive_index >= 48; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support -= 8 if public_climate_progressive_index < 48; news_headline = "The European ruling becomes the opening of a domestic marriage fight"

Lewica introduces equal marriage under Polish law instead of treating a
cross-border judgment as the destination. Equality organisations gain the bill
they asked for; PSL and the President prepare to stop it, and the right opens a
sovereignty campaign. Introduction begins the fight—it does not enact the right.

- @poland_event_queue: File the equal-marriage bill

@marriage_registry_truce
title: Implement recognition but declare a cultural truce on wider reform
subtitle: Legal compliance and centrist relations improve; the developmental-right path opens at a cost to progressives.
