= May 2025 — One flat, several answers

Days before the first round, <span class="party-pis"><b>Karol Nawrocki</b></span> is asked about a small Gdańsk
flat he acquired from an elderly, ill man in exchange for an undertaking of
care. The candidate has previously described owning one property. The seller
subsequently entered a municipal care institution; the care that was promised
is disputed; the account of the transaction changes twice in a week.

None of it is a criminal charge and none of it moves a single policy. It is a
character question in a campaign the right has built entirely on character:
the outsider, the historian, the man who is not a politician. He answers by
donating the flat, which resolves the property and not the question.

Our own candidate is **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]**, running on **[+
pres_2025_transfer_strategy +]** territory in a field where our path to a
runoff runs through people who dislike both leading candidates.

[? if left_dominant_current = "razem": Razem's people want the pensioner and
the care system in the story, not the candidate.?][? if left_dominant_current =
"social_patriot": Our social-patriotic organisers warn that a metropolitan
pile-on about property makes him sympathetic to exactly the voters we want.?]
[? if spring_path_route = "market_liberal": Our liberal turn makes an attack on
a property transaction sound like an attack on property.?]
[? if church_resolution_result = "Survivor testimony": The survivor network we
funded in 2023 already knows how to put a vulnerable person's account in front
of the country without turning them into campaign material.?]

- @nawrocki_flat_care
- @nawrocki_flat_character
- @nawrocki_flat_restraint
- @nawrocki_flat_network

@nawrocki_flat_care
title: Make it about the care system that let the seller end up in an institution
subtitle: Converts a campaign scandal into our own policy ground; slower to land than the personal attack.
on-arrival: health_policy_pressure += 8; pensioner_support += 3; public_trust += 3; labor_credibility += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Left answers the flat story with the care system behind it"

We put the actual question on the table: why does an ill man's care depend on
a private undertaking by a stranger, and how many thousand people are living
inside that arrangement right now because the state offers nothing else. The
candidate becomes one example rather than the subject.

It is the only version of this story that is still useful to us in July. It is
also considerably less exciting than the version everyone else is running, and
some of our own people would rather be running theirs.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the care argument into the last week

@nawrocki_flat_character
title: Join the character attack at full volume
subtitle: The most effective short-term damage to the right's candidate; it hands us a campaign fought entirely on personality.
on-arrival: pres_2025_right_credibility_hit += 1; pis_relation -= 6; left_poll_momentum += 0.25; public_trust += 1; ko_relation += 3; institutional_issue_salience -= 2; progressives_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Every opposition campaign runs the same week on the same flat"

We run it hard: the outsider who was going to clean up politics cannot give a
consistent account of how he came to own a sick man's flat. The clips are
excellent and the numbers move.

They move mostly between the two leading candidates. A campaign week spent on
character is a week in which nobody asks what any of them intends to do about
wages, and our own distinct offer is the thing that disappears from coverage.

- @poland_event_queue: Run the character week

@nawrocki_flat_restraint
title: Refuse the story and spend the week on our own programme
subtitle: Protects our distinct offer and forfeits the only week in which the right's candidate is genuinely vulnerable.
on-arrival: public_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.05; workers_support += 2; media_capacity -= 2; pis_relation += 2; progressives_dissent += 3; news_headline = "The Left declines the flat story and campaigns on wages instead"

Our candidate is asked about the flat at every stop and gives the same answer:
that is a matter for him and for the prosecutors if there is one, and here is
what we are proposing about rents. The discipline is total and the coverage is
minimal.

Whether this is integrity or malpractice depends entirely on the result. What
is certain is that the week in which the right's candidate was weakest is a
week we spent talking about something else.

- @poland_event_queue: Hold the programme line

@nawrocki_flat_network
title: Let the care organisations lead and keep the party's name off it
subtitle: Requires an established survivor and support network. The most credible version of the argument, and the one we get least credit for.
choose-if: church_resolution_result = "Survivor testimony" or movement_autonomy >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: We have no support network with the standing to lead this — a party press conference about a sick man's flat is a party press conference.
on-arrival: health_policy_pressure += 6; pensioner_support += 4; movement_autonomy += 5; public_trust += 4; media_capacity += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.1; pres_2025_right_credibility_hit += 1; news_headline = "Care organisations, not parties, put the pensioner's case to the country"

The organisations that spend every week arranging care for people in exactly
this position hold the press conference. We fund the room and stay out of the
photograph. What the country hears is not an attack on a candidate but a
description of a system in which a stranger's promise is the only care
available.

The candidate's answers get worse against that framing than against any
politician's question, because there is nobody to accuse of playing politics.
Our own poll numbers barely move, which is the price of the method working.

