= Late May 2025 — The interview nobody can refuse

Konfederacja's candidate **[+ pres_2025_konf_candidate +]** did not reach the
runoff. Party chair and broadcaster <span class="party-konf"><b>Sławomir
Mentzen</b></span> controls the programme through which that electorate now
decides. He does not endorse. He invites **[+ pres_2025_finalist_a +]**
and **[+ pres_2025_finalist_b +]** onto his own channel, separately, for long
unedited interviews in which each is asked to sign an eight-point declaration:
no new taxes, no restriction on cash, no ratification of the European
ceasefire-and-defence arrangements without a referendum, no limits on speech,
no Polish troops in Ukraine, and three further commitments written to be
uncomfortable for both of them.

This is not an endorsement market. It is a public examination of two
candidates by the party broker who has replaced the traditional broadcasters
as the place where the right-wing electorate decides, and it is watched by more
people than the televised debates.

[? if pres_2025_right_credibility_hit >= 2: The right's candidate arrives at
this interview already damaged by the property story, which is precisely why he
will sign anything put in front of him.?]
[? if pres_2025_player_finalist = 1: Our own candidate has been invited. The
invitation is not a courtesy and refusing it is a decision with a
number attached.?][? if pres_2025_player_finalist = 0: We are not in the
runoff. Our influence is limited to what we say about the process and to
whether the electorate we still hold treats a signature as disqualifying.?]

- @mentzen_expose_text
- @mentzen_contest_channel
- @mentzen_counter_offer

@mentzen_expose_text
title: Publish what each of the eight points actually costs
subtitle: Turns a loyalty ritual into a costed document; nobody in that audience is waiting for our arithmetic.
on-arrival: konf_normalisation -= 5; public_trust += 3; institutional_issue_salience += 3; media_capacity += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.1; news_headline = "The Left costs the eight points line by line"

We take the declaration seriously enough to price it: what a cash guarantee
does to tax enforcement, what a referendum lock does to defence financing,
what "no new taxes" means for the hospital budget of the person watching. The
document is answered as a programme, because that is what it is.

The audience it was written for is not reading our costings. Everyone who has
to govern afterwards is, and the signature becomes something a president can
be held to rather than a gesture that evaporates on inauguration day.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the costings

@mentzen_contest_channel
title: Attack the format: a private channel is not a national examination
subtitle: Defends broadcast pluralism and sounds exactly like the old media class the audience already rejected.
on-arrival: konf_normalisation += 4; media_capacity += 1; institutional_trust += 2; public_trust -= 1; konf_poll_momentum += 0.2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.05; news_headline = "The Left disputes a private channel's role as the runoff's examiner"

We say it plainly: an unregulated commercial channel with no obligation to
balance has become the venue where a presidential runoff is decided, and no
electoral rule covers it. The point is correct.

It is also delivered by a party asking to be trusted with the state, about a
man whose entire appeal is that the state's approved venues excluded people
like his audience. He plays the clip himself, twice.

- @poland_event_queue: File the format objection

@mentzen_counter_offer
title: Offer his voters the two points where we actually agree
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Takes the parts of the declaration a left party can honestly sign and refuses the rest in public.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party has no capacity to run a separate appeal into that audience.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; konf_normalisation -= 3; anti_system_trust += 4; workers_support += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; progressives_dissent += 5; spring_dissent += 3; public_trust += 1; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Left signs two of the eight points and rejects six on the record"

Speech protections and the limit on committing troops are positions we hold
already and have held longer than he has. We sign those two publicly, name the
six we refuse and why, and take the argument to the audience rather than
around it.

Our progressive organisers hate the photograph. Some of the young men who left
us for him in 2023 listen to a Left answer for the first time in two years,
which is either the beginning of a recovery or the first step of becoming a
softer version of the thing we oppose.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the two signatures

